@page "/docs/components/popover"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Popover
<PageTitle>Popover - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Popover</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="popover" />
        </div>
        <p>A floating panel anchored to a trigger and positioned with <a class="font-medium text-foreground" href="https://floating-ui.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Floating UI</a>, so it flips to stay in view. It is <strong>non-modal</strong>: the rest of the page stays interactive while it is open, and an outside click both closes the popover and acts on whatever you clicked. Escape dismisses it too.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(PopoverDefaultExample)"
                Description="After importing `Blaizio.Ui`, a trigger and a content panel are all you need. With `RenderAs`, any element can be the trigger." />

    <CompositionTree Root="Anatomy"
                     Description="Every part of a popover. The title and description go in a header, `BzPopoverArrow` is optional, and `BzPopoverClose` dismisses the popover from inside." />

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Portaling</h2>
        <p>While open, the panel moves itself to the document body, so no ancestor stacking context or overflow clip can cover or cut it, whether that is a fixed sidebar, a transformed card or a scroll container. Positioning, focus and dismissal work the same either way.</p>
        <p>Set <code>Inline="true"</code> to render it in place instead, which helps under CSS containment, for print, or in tests that assert on nearby markup. Because the portaled panel leaves its ancestors behind, their CSS selectors cannot reach it, so style it through its own <code>Class</code> or slot attributes.</p>
    </section>

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Description="Click the trigger to open the panel and move focus into it. Clicking outside or pressing Escape closes it and returns focus to the trigger."
          Example="typeof(PopoverDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom trigger element (RenderAs)"
          Description="If the trigger should be a link, a card or one of your own components, use `RenderAs` and apply the attributes it provides to that element."
          Example="typeof(PopoverRenderAsTriggerExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Arrow" Description="Add a `BzPopoverArrow` inside the content to point back at the trigger. It shares the panel's fill, ring and shadow so it reads as part of the panel, and it turns to face the trigger from whichever side the panel opens on."
          Example="typeof(PopoverArrowExample)" />

    <Demo Title="With a form" Description="The panel can hold inputs, buttons and any other interactive content. Widen it with a `Class` on `BzPopoverContent`."
          Example="typeof(PopoverFormExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Align" Description="`Align` sets where the panel sits along the trigger's edge: start, center or end."
          Example="typeof(PopoverAlignExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Sides" Description="`Side` sets the preferred edge the panel opens from. If there is not enough room, it flips to the opposite side to stay in view."
          Example="typeof(PopoverSidesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Controlled" Description="Bind `Open` to a field when your page needs to open or close the popover itself. `BzPopoverClose` still closes it from inside the panel."
          Example="typeof(PopoverControlledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Every part accepts `Class`. This example gives the trigger a brand color and the panel a tinted surface, an accent border and a wider radius."
          Example="typeof(PopoverCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the panel anchors and aligns from the opposite side."
          Example="typeof(PopoverRtlExample)" />

</div>

@code {
    // The anatomy drawn by the Composition section - CompositionTree computes the connectors.
    private static readonly CompositionNode Anatomy = new("BzPopover",
        new CompositionNode("BzPopoverTrigger"),
        new CompositionNode("BzPopoverContent",
            new CompositionNode("BzPopoverHeader",
                new CompositionNode("BzPopoverTitle"),
                new CompositionNode("BzPopoverDescription")),
            new CompositionNode("BzPopoverArrow"),
            new CompositionNode("BzPopoverClose")));
}
